"""Evidence-qualified historical associations; distinct from modern chemistry."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
entries=[]
def add(sp,common,association,evidence,period,url,confidence,description,scope):
 entries.append(dict(scientific_name=sp,common_name=common,association=association,evidence_type=evidence,period=period,source_url=url,citation=url,confidence=confidence,description=description,taxonomic_scope=scope))
pmc=lambda n:'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/'+n+'/'
saqqara=pmc('PMC9908542');textiles=pmc('PMC6832961');perfume='https://doi.org/10.1086/715345'
add('Boswellia spp.','Frankincense','Embalming material interpretation','FTIR on mummy skin, hair and wig','New Kingdom context, TT71 area (1479–1458 BCE)',pmc('PMC11328696'),'Moderate; material-level assignment','FTIR was interpreted as frankincense with juniper resin. This method does not establish a Boswellia species or a complete recipe. Modern B. carterii chemistry is stored separately.','Genus/material only; species unresolved')
add('Commiphora spp.','Myrrh','Perfumery and ritual textual interpretation','Classical/Egyptian textual comparison and experimental archaeology','Ptolemaic/Roman textual and Mendesian perfume context',perfume,'Moderate; historical interpretation','The Mendesian perfume reconstruction uses myrrh. Ancient terminology and modern species assignment require caution; a reconstructed recipe is not direct proof of each ingredient in Cleopatra’s perfume.','Commiphora resin interpretation; no ancient C. myrrha species determination')
add('Ricinus communis','Castor','Embalming workshop preparation','GC-MS organic residue analysis','26th Dynasty, Saqqara, 664–525 BCE',saqqara,'Moderate; probable oil identification','Ricinoleic-acid patterns were interpreted as castor oil in workshop residues. Degradation and mixture context constrain inference; not evidence that the free acid was the original whole oil.','Probable castor oil; biomarker-based')
add('Sesamum indicum','Sesame','Candidate ancient oil-bearing crop','Proteomics primary study with archaeological synthesis','Second millennium BCE / New Kingdom reference context',pmc('PMC7812755'),'Moderate for regional crop; indirect for Egypt','The primary proteomics results concern Levantine dental calculus. The discussion regards Tutankhamun-tomb sesame seeds as credible based on prior archaeobotany. This is indirect Egyptian evidence, not Egyptian oil residue identification.','Species-supported regional proteins; Egyptian claim derives from cited archaeobotany')
add('Linum usitatissimum','Flax','Funerary linen textiles','Microscopy and chemical study of museum archaeological textiles','Pharaonic to Ptolemaic; individual textile dates in source Table 1',textiles,'High for linen use; oil use not tested','Flax-derived linen shrouds and mummy textiles establish botanical/funerary use. They do not demonstrate that linseed oil was used as an embalming ingredient.','Flax textile fibres; modern seed-oil profiles separate')
add('Carthamus tinctorius','Safflower','Funerary textile dye','HPLC-MS carthamin/degradation-product identification','Pharaonic Egyptian museum textiles; sample dates in Table 1',textiles,'High for dye material; oil use not tested','Six textile samples contained safflower dye markers. This supports dye use and funerary textiles, not sacred status or safflower oil use.','Carthamus dye material')
add('Balanites aegyptiaca','Desert Date','Mendesian perfume reconstruction candidate','Experimental archaeology and historical oil-name interpretation','Classical Mendesian perfume tradition',perfume,'Moderate; botanical name interpretation','Balanos is evaluated in the perfume reconstruction literature. Historical plant-name translation and reconstruction are less specific than direct botanical remains; modern kernel-oil data do not establish ancient use.','Balanos / desert-date interpretation; uncertainty retained')
add('Nymphaea caerulea','Blue Egyptian Lily','Ptolemaic Bes-vessel botanical association','Multianalytical residue study including plant DNA','Ptolemaic-style Bes vase; original find context unrecorded',pmc('PMC11561246'),'Moderate; context and taxonomic limitations','The study reports Nymphaea nouchali var. caerulea in a museum Bes vessel. Ritual and psychoactive interpretations are hypotheses; the vessel lacks a secure excavated provenance. No synthetic modern chemical profile was added.','Source taxon N. nouchali var. caerulea / N. caerulea synonym context')
add('Juniperus spp. / Cupressus spp.','Juniper / Cypress','Embalming preparation','GC-MS organic residue analysis','26th Dynasty, Saqqara, 664–525 BCE',saqqara,'High for conifer preparation; unresolved genus pair','Biomarkers support juniper/cypress oil or tar in workshop preparations. They do not securely separate these genera or establish J. phoenicea as the ancient species.','Juniperus/Cupressus unresolved; modern J. phoenicea reference separate')
add('Cedrus spp.','Cedar','Embalming tar','GC-MS chemomarkers in canopic-jar residues','Late Period, 664–332 BCE',pmc('PMC13144440'),'High for cedar-derived material; species unresolved','Cedar tar marker patterns were detected in two canopic jars. Modern C. atlantica tar was a reference; this does not identify ancient cedar to that species.','Cedrus genus; no ancient species assignment')
add('Olea europaea','Olive','Probable plant-oil preparation','GC-MS organic residue analysis','26th Dynasty, Saqqara, 664–525 BCE',saqqara,'Moderate; probable oil type','Plant oil interpreted as olive-type is reported among workshop preparations. Common fatty-acid patterns, degradation and mixtures limit species specificity.','Probable olive-type oil; not species-exclusive biomarkers')
add('Moringa peregrina','Moringa peregrina','Baq-oil historical identification candidate','Historical oil-name interpretation; no direct molecular species proof','Ancient Egyptian oil texts, chronology varies',pmc('PMC7812755'),'Uncertain; candidate only','The source discussion explicitly notes that baq oil may refer to olive, moringa or another oil plant. No secure M. peregrina-specific ancient residue identification is claimed. Modern Omani seed-lipid data remain separate.','Candidate Moringa identification; cannot substitute M. oleifera')
path=Path('data/literature/heritage_manifest.json');path.write_text(json.dumps({'format':1,'category':'Ancient Egyptian Botanical Heritage','policy':'Historical associations are evidence-qualified; no blanket sacred designation. Modern analytical profiles are not evidence of ancient species or recipes.','entries':entries},ensure_ascii=False,indent=2),encoding='utf-8');print(len(entries),'historical candidate evaluations')
